  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340724",
      "title": "Showing a \"Loading\" Fallback",
      "lectureOrder": 162,
      "videoOrder": 150,
      "sourceHash": "ec35e073fef4da373ae944252d90fab0dc92cea0dd4bee5dad34f7442a33f992",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.24,
          "en": "Now, this is now the best way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.24,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "of fetching data in a NextJS application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 12.11,
          "en": "if you own the data source, so if you own the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "If you have an external API, you, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "will need to send an HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 20.19,
          "en": "but if you own the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.19,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "you can move it into your NextJS project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 25.593,
          "en": "and reach out to it like we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.52,
          "end": 29.67,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned, the nice thing about SQLite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.67,
          "end": 31.41,
          "en": "and the package we're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "is that it's actually a synchronous package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 37.59,
          "en": "and we don't even need to use async await,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.59,
          "end": 42.59,
          "en": "but I actually wanna simulate a slower response here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 45.434,
          "en": "and therefore, I will actually turn this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.434,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "into an async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "even though the SQL package we're using would not need it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "but I'll add async here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "so that I can then await a new promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 62.1,
          "en": "which I only add here so that I can add a short delay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 63.438,
          "en": "because I also wanna show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.438,
          "end": 67.41,
          "en": "how to handle loading states, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.41,
          "end": 71.31,
          "en": "So this promise constructor gets a function as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "which automatically receives a resolve function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "and then here, I'll simply call set timeout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 80.07,
          "en": "and I'll set a timeout of two seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.07,
          "end": 83.463,
          "en": "and resolve should be triggered after these two seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.84,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "and I await this promise then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "So this will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 91.59,
          "en": "that we simply add a two-second delay here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.59,
          "end": 95.25,
          "en": "to simulate a slower backend process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.25,
          "end": 99.33,
          "en": "or simulate a database that's slower, because again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.33,
          "end": 102.813,
          "en": "I wanna show you how to handle loading states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.00999999999999,
          "en": "With that, now that we're using async await here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.00999999999999,
          "end": 110.53399999999999,
          "en": "get all news does no longer directly return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.53399999999999,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "an array of news, but instead, it'll now return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "which will eventually yield an array of news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "Therefore, the code in the page.js file must be adjusted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 128.583,
          "en": "because we can no longer call get all news like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "But that's no problem, because as I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 134.76,
          "en": "and showed you before already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.76,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "you can decorate your component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "with async if they're React server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 142.203,
          "en": "which this one is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.28,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "So hence, we can simply add await here, and we're good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 149.673,
          "en": "That's all we have to do to fetch those news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.9,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "If we now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 155.754,
          "en": "we still get that page with the news, but actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.754,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "you will see that if you're on a different page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "and you reload there to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 165.69,
          "en": "that NextJS loses its cache and you click on news again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.69,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "nothing seems to happen initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.77,
          "en": "and then only once the data is there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.77,
          "end": 171.603,
          "en": "do we navigate to this page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 173.91,
          "en": "This does not happen thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.91,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "because NextJS actually caches this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "but it happens during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "if you reload some other page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 183.81,
          "en": "and then try to go back to news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.81,
          "end": 186.72,
          "en": "And that's, of course, not a great user experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.72,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "because it seems as if nothing's happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "after clicking on news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 193.683,
          "en": "until we suddenly switch to that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.64,
          "end": 197.85,
          "en": "It would be better to show some loading fallback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.85,
          "end": 199.703,
          "en": "some loading spinner or loading text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.703,
          "end": 204.703,
          "en": "or some skeleton loader until the data is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.78,
          "end": 207.433,
          "en": "and adding such a loading fallback, thankfully,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.433,
          "end": 211.59,
          "en": "is pretty straightforward in NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.59,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "You can add a special file called loading.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "next to the page that is loading data or on a higher level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "and NextJS will automatically show the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 226.74,
          "en": "of the component defined in this loading.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.74,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "until the data is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 233.52,
          "en": "So here, I can export my new function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.52,
          "end": 237.21,
          "en": "news loading or whatever you wanna call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.21,
          "end": 239.88,
          "en": "and maybe just return this fallback text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.88,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "though you could, of course, return any JSX content here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 246.633,
          "en": "a loading spinner, whatever you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.1,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "Here, I'll keep it simple and just return this loading text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 255.12,
          "en": "and with this loading.js file added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.12,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "it'll take care of showing us this loading text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 261.723,
          "en": "if a sibling or child page is loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 264.33,
          "en": "So therefore, now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 267.364,
          "en": "if I go back to archive and reload and then click on news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.364,
          "end": 271.41,
          "en": "we go there instantly, and we see that loading fallback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.41,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "And that's, of course, now a better user experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "because now we got that instant navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "and we know what's going on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 282.15,
          "en": "We understand that we're simply waiting for data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.15,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "and that is how easy it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 287.537,
          "en": "to add a loading fallback with NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
